meta {
  name: 05_AuthorizationNegatives
  seq: 5
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Scenario: The log is refused to everyone who may not read it for the party

    When the delegator reads its own log with direction=via
    Then it is refused
    And an unknown direction is refused
    And an empty party is refused
    And a party that is not a uuid is refused
    And a party that does not exist is refused
    And a token with an unrelated scope is refused
    And an enterprise token is refused
    And the service owner cannot read an enduser's request log
    And a token that is not a JWT is rejected with 401
    And a private person cannot read the Maskinporten log
    And filter values without a direction are refused

  Every refusal is a 403 with no body, except the token that is not a JWT, which fails
  authentication with 401. The party and direction checks run in authorization, before the
  query is validated, which is why a bad party or direction is 403 and not 400.

  Which scope reads which direction is covered by the controller integration tests
  (ActivityLogControllerTest), which run on every pull request. This scenario keeps the
  checks that depend on the deployed environment: the party authorization against the
  real authorization service, and the token types.
}
